{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790432051,"nonce":"X71ebIa/MIOsgI84wub6h5I4oQE=","message":"Embedding (caribou asked): wlift_runtime.o and the aot_runtime staticlib define no entry: no _start, main or __main_void. The bootstrap is emitted by llvm_aot into the program object. Under caribou, Haxe's main drives and caribou-wren owns the VM (made on caribou's heap seam), so a WrenLift program object must not define __main_void or make its own VM.\n\nPlanned shape: an entry option on the LLVM AOT build. Main (default, standalone) emits __main_void / main as now. Library emits the same bootstrap body as `wlift_program_run(vm) -\u003e i32`: it takes the host's VM, fills the tables, installs classes and closures, runs the module bodies, and returns 0 or the uncaught-error code. No new_vm, no free_vm. The program's internal symbols are already Internal linkage, so only wlift_program_run is exported (namespaced per program if a host links several). Not needed until caribou 3bfe4a0 builds its object.","files":null}]}